# Frontend design

Read and follow `.cursor/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md` before changing UI.

Emulocke visual direction is **graphite clamshell**: matte graphite chassis, inset screen wells, parchment-metal hairlines (`#D7CDBD`), metal text on dark, scarce crimson for pause only. Type is M PLUS Rounded 1c for display and Fira Sans for body. Blocky DS geometry. Not cream command boxes. Not stock ImGui gray. Not purple gradients. Not Inter/Roboto/Arial/system UI fonts.

Screens sit in bezels. Console hugs integer-scaled pixels with a 5px DS hinge and 21px graphite around the cluster. Suite is a tab bar; Logs is first. Integer-scale nearest-neighbor for emulator pixels. No scanlines. No fake tracker widgets. Red is pause and destructive, not hover.
